[ceiling] The closed splash-baffle floor bridges the 9 mm chamber and the 3 mm side-slot mouths when the lid prints exterior-face down. The four retained wall sectors join that floor to the plate. This is the reviewed splash barrier below the open tube tip; printed bridge finish remains unqualified.
alternatives: An open floor loses the upward-splash barrier. A conical floor changes the reviewed 3 mm drop and tube-tip clearance; a support requiring removal through the 3 × 2 mm slots has no established removal result.
